  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Empty Bottle in Chicago, IL, on Thursday, November 15, 2007 [1][2]. This audience recording, captured by Peter Sohriakoff and transferred by Mike Wojciechowski, is the only available recording of this specific show [1]. The setlist includes tracks such as \"Wild Sage,\" \"Hath Thou Considered The Tetrapod,\" \"Quito,\" and \"In the Craters on the Moon\" [1]. The performance also features \"Mole,\" \"You or Your Memory,\" \"Maybe Sprout Wings,\" \"Dance Music,\" \"Color in Your Cheeks,\" and \"See America Right\" [1]. Notably, the recording contains the first archived performance of \"Sept 15, 1983\" [1]. The encore section includes \"We Bite,\" which is noted as the only archived performance of that song, with Jon Wurster providing vocals on one take and Peter Hughes on another [1]. The encore concludes with \"Houseguest,\" \"California Song,\" and \"The Best Ever Death Metal Band in Denton\" [1]. This show is the 115th in the archive's collection for the performer, following a previous archived show on November 3, 2007, at The Slowdown [2]. The recording runs for 69 minutes and contains 17 songs [1].",
